Always read the current revision and recent accepted changes before interpreting relative references. Resolve real object IDs, never fabricated indices. Record baseRevision, userRequest, targetSet, preserveSet, changeSet, validation and newRevision. Unmentioned objects, assets, copy and audio are preserved. Captions do not imply narration. A bound narration edit alone may synchronize its captions. Resolve “往上” against the last unambiguous edited object; ask one question only if the current project and history cannot disambiguate. Selective restoration copies only requested properties from real revision ancestry; never restores the entire document for an audio/transition request. Publish only after target/preserve validation and preview checks; failed explicit effects are never replaced.

